        {
          "path": "_m/w/9/4/d/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-wp/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-1193.jpg",
          "filename": "Kota Kinabalu City Mosque (11931321805).jpg",
          "caption": "After bringing me to this beautiful structure, the KK City Mosque, my guide wanted to take a break to pray. Fair enough, he had been driving me around since early morning, and he needed a break as well. I had about half an hour to explore the place, but being a religious house of prayer, I did not follow him into the mosque or walk around too much. While notes appear in subsequent photographs, here is a far shot of the City Mosque reflecting in the beautiful pool surrounding it. Yes, Malaysia is an Islamic country. (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "alt": "After bringing me to this beautiful structure, the KK City Mosque, my guide wanted to take a break to pray. Fair enough, he had been driving me around since early morning, and he needed a break as well. I had about half an hour to explore the place, but being a religious house of prayer, I did not follow him into the mosque or walk around too much. While notes appear in subsequent photographs, here is a far shot of the City Mosque reflecting in the beautiful pool surrounding it. Yes, Malaysia is an Islamic country. (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "width": 2848,
          "height": 4288,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kota_Kinabalu_City_Mosque_(11931321805).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "w94d",
          "mediumPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-wp/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-1193-medium.webp",
          "smallPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-wp/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-1193-small.webp"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/w/9/4/d/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-wp/kota-kinabalu-city-mosque-1193-1.jpg",
          "filename": "Kota Kinabalu City Mosque (11931782614).jpg",
          "caption": "Here is another long shot of the beautiful KK City Mosque, this time in landscape mode. Built on a 2.47 acres site at the Likas bay, the Kota Kinabalu City Mosque is exemplary of the Islamic contemporary architecture. Situated near the sea, this majestic white mosque boasts similar features to the Nabawi Mosque in Medina. This floating mosque has a prayer hall which houses three madrasahs and accommodates from 9, 000 to 12, 000 people at a time.  (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "alt": "Here is another long shot of the beautiful KK City Mosque, this time in landscape mode. Built on a 2.47 acres site at the Likas bay, the Kota Kinabalu City Mosque is exemplary of the Islamic contemporary architecture. Situated near the sea, this majestic white mosque boasts similar features to the Nabawi Mosque in Medina. This floating mosque has a prayer hall which houses three madrasahs and accommodates from 9, 000 to 12, 000 people at a time.  (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "width": 4288,
